model2recomp — third-party attribution
======================================

model2recomp is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). Large parts of the hardware model
are *ports* of MAME code, and a port is a derivative work: those files stay
under MAME's BSD-3-Clause licence, with the original copyright intact. They
are other people's work and are credited as such.

Without MAME's Model 2 driver this library could not exist. The Model 2's
geometry engine, colour path, and I/O board were reverse-engineered by the
people named below over two decades; nothing here re-derived any of it.


